description:
FOUND s513f (Opus, 2026-10-10) reading the CPAN board: Role-Tiny role-basic-composition.t row 34 'role method applied' (got 'My::Class::Base method', expected 'My::Does::Basic1 method').  The row became REACHABLE in s513f (on main the file stops at row 3: line 59 `is My::Class2->method2, ...` was refused 'statement not supported'); the bug itself is PRE-EXISTING -- the minimal probe below answers the same on main decda07f and on the s513f tree.

REPRODUCER (scratch/s513f/pr/rt.pl in the s513f worktree):
    use lib "<Role-Tiny>/lib"; require Role::Tiny;
    { package My::Does::Basic1; use Role::Tiny; requires 'turbo_charger'; sub method { __PACKAGE__ . ' method' } }
    { package My::Does::Conflict; use Role::Tiny; sub method { __PACKAGE__ . ' method' } }
    { package My::Class::Base; sub turbo_charger { 1 } sub method { __PACKAGE__ . ' method' } }
    eval q{ package My::Class::Child; use base 'My::Class::Base'; use Role::Tiny::With; with qw/My::Does::Basic1 My::Does::Conflict/; 1 };
    eval q{ package My::Class::Child2; use base 'My::Class::Base'; use Role::Tiny::With; with qw/My::Does::Basic1/; 1 };
    print My::Class::Child2->method, "\n";
perl 5.40.3: My::Does::Basic1 method.  PCL: My::Class::Base method.  Without the first (conflict) composition PCL is right -- so state left by the first composition (Role::Tiny's per-role method caches, or a stub / glob installed in a package, or PCL's method cache) decides the second.  Measure first: dump Role::Tiny's $INFO / $APPLIED_TO after each eval under perl and PCL, and whether Child2::method exists as a glob after the second.
